<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jagaddipendra Narayan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1915–1970</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jagaddipendra Narayan was the last ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Cooch Behar, succeeding as a child in 1922 and ruling in his own right from 1936. A noted sportsman, he served in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. In August 1949 he signed the agreement merging Cooch Behar with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and it became a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a> in 1950.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jagaddipendra-narayan.jpg" alt="Jagaddipendra Narayan" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jagaddipendra_Narayan_at_his_coronation,_c._1936.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
